audio/alsa: do not poll for device hotplug

SDL's ALSA backend starts a thread that re-enumerates every PCM device via
snd_device_name_hint() every 5 seconds to synthesize hotplug events. On the
F1C200s that enumeration (alsa.conf parsing for one soldered-in codec)
costs ~300 ms of a 408 MHz core per scan -- 6% CPU measured with
/proc/<tid>/sched while FastCarPlay plays music -- for an event that can
never happen on a head unit with a fixed codec. SDL's own comment on the
switch: "without the thread, you will detect devices on startup, but will
not get further hotplug events. But that might be okay." It is.

--- a/src/audio/alsa/SDL_alsa_audio.c
+++ b/src/audio/alsa/SDL_alsa_audio.c
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
 
 /* without the thread, you will detect devices on startup, but will not get futher hotplug events. But that might be okay. */
 #ifndef SDL_ALSA_HOTPLUG_THREAD
-#define SDL_ALSA_HOTPLUG_THREAD 1
+#define SDL_ALSA_HOTPLUG_THREAD 0
 #endif
 
 /* Allow access to a raw mixing buffer */
